  "about": "Chapter 1 beat 8 and its gate (Book 4 section 08; Book 6 section 15; Book 2 section 16; Stage 12, decisions S12-1 to S12-25): the launch. It opens once the boat is seaworthy and the three searches are decided; looking the boat over then offers to launch it, which opens the readiness screen (the boat, the tide, the crew, the stores, the weapons in hand, allies and Thorkel's rites), with its point-of-no-return warning. Confirmed, it makes the labelled checkpoint and asks the boat's name and its sail's mark; then the household runs the boat down its skids into the water, climbs aboard, sets the sail and rows out, and the sea map shows the coast and smoke rising at Carrick Landing. Closing the map ends Chapter 1: the trial row's time passes, the boat is drawn up again, and the chapter-end save is made. Positions are tiles in the strand's own map; the scene's seconds are its choreography (like the opening's, decision S6-5); every tuning number is Book 10's (section 22, The launch).",
